decode a missing Swift class as the ancestor the archive names

iA Writer logged this once a run and lost an object every time:

  Failed to decode an instance of class _TtGCs26_SwiftDeferredNSDictionarySSP__: class not found

That is a Swift Dictionary<String, Any> bridged into a keyed archive. The generic specialisation
cannot be looked up by name here, so the whole object came back NIL and the caller got nothing.

$classes IS THE ANSWER AND IT WAS ALREADY BEING READ, only to check that it exists. It lists the
class and its ancestors precisely so a reader that lacks the leaf can decode it as one of them, and
for a bridged collection the ancestor IS the payload. Darwin raises in this position because Darwin
always has the leaf.

THREE ATTEMPTS AT ONE CHAIN, and the first two are worth recording because they replaced a silent
nil with a dead process:

  _TtGCs26_SwiftDeferredNSDictionarySSP__, Swift.__SwiftNativeNSDictionary,
  __SwiftNativeNSDictionaryBase, NSDictionary

  1  take the first name that resolves      Swift.__SwiftNativeNSDictionary resolves, and it is an
                                            abstract base in libswiftCore: "count requires a
                                            subclass implementation", 2 runs of 2 terminated.
  2  skip Swift. and _Tt by name            __SwiftNativeNSDictionaryBase has neither prefix. Same
                                            exception, 3 runs of 3. The names do not share a
                                            prefix and a blacklist was going to keep growing.
  3  skip a class the SWIFT RUNTIME         class_getImageName says the thing that actually
     IMPLEMENTS                             matters: an abstract Swift shim only works on an
                                            instance the Swift runtime built. An application's own
                                            Swift classes live in its own binary and are untouched.

MEASURED, iA Writer

  before  1 class not found per run, object dropped
  after   0 in 3, 0 faults, 0 terminations

WHAT DID NOT CHANGE. The library rows still say Updating... This removes a decode that silently
returned nil; it is not what the rows are waiting for.
